It reads the water tests of the user's own LabCom account (the cloud of the
Water-i.d. PoolLab 1.0 / 2.0 and PrimeLab photometers) through the official
LabCom GraphQL API (https://backend.labcom.cloud/graphql), with a personal API
token created by the user on labcom.cloud. This integration is not affiliated
with nor endorsed by Water-i.d. GmbH. The query follows the published GraphQL
schema; the field names were compared with the Home Assistant client
"python_poollab" (https://github.com/dala318/python_poollab, MIT) and the
ioBroker adapter "ioBroker.labcom" (https://github.com/100prznt/ioBroker.labcom,
MIT). No code and no test data are taken from either: test/fixtures/cloud.json
is a made-up account.
